{"channel":"edge","issued_at":"2026-10-30T09:15:02Z","items":[{"approvals":{"approvers":["snapshot"],"pull_request":1},"archive":{"name":"3e2aa79f-9d73-48fd-839e-ccf1525b42e7-1.0.0.zip","sha256":"e08c894b4cac412eaf772418654afe55b611bf8b3cb4c9ffb99f7bb0e9db42f4","size":126153},"category":"attack-scenario","description":"EASM is a cybersecurity practice focused on discovering, mapping, and continuously monitoring all internet-facing assets of an organization (websites, IP addresses, cloud services, APIs, admin portals, etc.).\n\nThe goal is to take the attacker’s perspective in order to identify vulnerabilities, misconfigurations, or forgotten services before they can be exploited.\n\nKey challenges:\n\n- Eliminating blind spots (shadow IT, unmanaged services)\n-  Detecting vulnerabilities (CVEs) and risky configurations early\n- Maintaining a strong security posture in a constantly evolving IT environment\n\nSimply define an asset using an IP address or FQDN. OpenAEV then performs enumeration just like an attacker would:\n- Identifying open ports and running services\n- Detecting exposed administration portals\n- Checking for known vulnerabilities (CVEs)\n- Highlighting misconfigurations (e.g., default credentials)\n- Findings are correlated and reported, giving clear visibility into external exposure.","external_id":"3e2aa79f-9d73-48fd-839e-ccf1525b42e7","main_focus":"endpoint-protection","name":"EASM Scenario","payloads":[],"platforms":["Generic"],"requires":{"edition":"CE","executors":[],"injectors":["openaev_nmap","openaev_nuclei"],"openaev":">=3.261005.0"},"severity":"high","status":"VERIFIED","tabletop":false,"threat":{"ttps":["T1595","T1595.002","T1046"]},"type":"time-based","version":"1.0.0"},{"approvals":{"approvers":["snapshot"],"pull_request":1},"archive":{"name":"f43a1c51-f4e6-4bad-9d41-1858bdde0888-1.0.0.zip","sha256":"be41155478485add55c5990bd8ad5bd2e044cf9c7fd647c854eb403dd924ec0b","size":55669},"category":"attack-scenario","description":"List the runn